    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing righties. **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) leads the charge as our premier play; a fantastic matchup against Adams, M (4.57 xERA) paired with favorable park factors pushes his score into the elite tier, and we expect him to capitalize on his elite sprint speed. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **James Wood** (72.52) follow closely behind. **Mickey Moniak** benefits immensely from the 5.11 xERA of Kelly, while **James Wood** overcomes a tough lefty-lefty matchup through pure xwOBA dominance and an advantageous leadoff spot. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) and **Josh Naylor** (69.11) round out the top of our high-efficiency cohort, both benefiting from the 5.08 xERA of Pecko.\n\nThe bench decision process was competitive, with **Travis Bazzana** (46.68) narrowly missing the cut. While his platoon edge against Gray is notable, the optimizer preferred the superior SP-specific matchups afforded to our starters. We are wary of the \"Wind In\" warnings affecting **Brice Turang**, **Trevor Story**, **Austin Riley**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Seiya Suzuki**; these conditions have dampened their projected scores, necessitating vigilance if mid-game weather reports shift. Additionally, with lineup status still pending for several starters like **Gabriel Moreno**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Brice Turang**, **Trevor Story**, **Cole Young**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Josh Naylor**, we remain flexible to swap in **Griffin Conine** or **Vinnie Pasquantino** if a preferred starter sits. Finally, we remain without **Giancarlo Stanton**, who continues to occupy an IL slot.",
